{
  // Build-only project. `pnpm build` runs `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`, so the
  // runtime artifact (dist/) contains ONLY runtime code.
  //
  // WHY a second file instead of adding these excludes to tsconfig.json: that
  // file is the editor/typecheck project, and `pnpm typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`)
  // must keep type-checking the tests. Excluding them there would silently drop
  // 24 test files out of type coverage.
  //
  // WHY exclude tests from the build at all: dist/ is now compiled at image
  // build time and shipped in the image. A compiled dist/test/**/*.js copy of
  // each test would be globbed by vitest alongside its TypeScript source
  // (`include: ['**/**/*.integration.{js,ts}']`) and fails immediately --
  // "Vitest cannot be imported in a CommonJS module using require()" -- because
  // tsc emits CommonJS. It would also ship test code and upload test sourcemaps
  // to Sentry. Nothing outside src/test imports test code, so the runtime is
  // unaffected: dist/index.js and every module it requires still emit here.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist",
    "build",
    ".docker-build",
    "src/test",
    "**/*.test.ts",
    "**/*.integration.ts"
  ]
}
